THOUGHT: I should mirror the null-handling pattern used in when(T methodCall): check if pullOngoingStubbing() returned null, and if so reset mockingProgress and throw the same missingMethodInvocation() error. I’ll update getLastInvocation() accordingly and then run the build to confirm that the NullAway error is resolved and no new ones appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/mockito && sed -i '253,258c\  public Invocation getLastInvocation() {
    MockingProgress mockingProgress = mockingProgress();
    OngoingStubbingImpl ongoingStubbing =
        (OngoingStubbingImpl) mockingProgress.pullOngoingStubbing();
    if (ongoingStubbing == null) {
      mockingProgress.reset();
      throw missingMethodInvocation();
    }
    List<Invocation> allInvocations = ongoingStubbing.getRegisteredInvocations();
    return allInvocations.get(allInvocations.size() - 1);
  }' src/main/java/org/mockito/internal/MockitoCore.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "MockitoCore.java" new_build_output.log || true```

